# Baked icon recipe -- the single source of truth for BakedIcons.g.cs.
#
# Regenerate with:  pwsh tools/bake-icons.ps1
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The generated .g.cs carries a "re-run the tool" banner, but the ARGUMENTS are the part that matters
# and they lived only in a shell history. So the table could not actually be regenerated without
# knowing which glyphs, from which font, at which sizes. It is data rather than script so the build can
# watch it (warning TWIC0001 fires when this file is newer than the generated table) and so a future
# generator could read the same thing.
#
# WHY BAKE AT ALL
# A mark drawn from a font at RUNTIME is absent where the face is not installed, and a missing glyph
# draws NOTHING rather than a placeholder, so a button's only mark silently disappears. It also cannot
# be tinted when the face is colour, so it cannot dim with the label beside it. Baked coverage is
# monochrome and identical on every host.
#
# NOT EVERY GLYPH SURVIVES, AND THE FAILURES ALL LOOK THE SAME: a solid rectangle. The bake keeps the
# ALPHA silhouette, so a glyph whose structure is drawn in COLOUR collapses. Measured at 13 px against
# this font, all of these came out fully inked and were rejected:
#     U+1F4C2 folder      U+1F3AF crosshair    U+1F9EE abacus
#     U+1F522 input-nums  U+23EB  double-up
# Verify a candidate by baking it and printing the mask. In a colour preview every one of the above
# looks like a perfectly good icon.
#
# LICENSING: baking redistributes glyph OUTLINES, so the font below must permit that. Noto is OFL. A
# proprietary system face (seguiemj) is never a valid source, even though a runtime probe may
# legitimately fall back to one.

# Settings. Paths are relative to THIS file, so the recipe is self-contained.
font      = ../TianWen.UI.Gui/Fonts/Noto-COLRv1.ttf
output    = BakedIcons.g.cs
namespace = TianWen.UI.Abstractions

# Sizes are deliberately omitted: the tool's default ladder is one bake per common DPI scale for a
# 13-unit mark, and restating it here would be a second copy free to drift from it.

# Glyphs. Name => codepoint; the name becomes the generated field. Each says what it is FOR, because a
# bare codepoint records nothing about why it earned a bake.
Spiral     = U+1F300   # Objects overlay. Three hand-drawn attempts failed first: an outline with
                       # anything inside it reads as an EYE at 13 px, whatever the inner shape is.
Sparkles   = U+2728    # AI enhance. Lets the label drop its "AI: " prefix and show only the backend.
Magnifier  = U+1F50D   # Zoom. What makes the tri-state Fit / 1:1 / 43% label affordable.
Telescope  = U+1F52D   # Plate solve: work out where this frame is pointing.
HeavyCheck = U+2714    # Kept baked as a FALLBACK for a solved plate solve. The label draws this as text
                       # now that the viewer bundles DejaVu Sans, which carries it; before that it
                       # resolved Consolas, which has no check mark, so the tick drew nothing. Note
                       # U+2713 (plain check) is absent from Noto, so heavy check is the one in both.
